I'd hope that's true, the major fun in the tournament for a lot of us
is seeing how the upper-echelon players do.  Or to put another way,
Wimbledon seems biased toward the upper echelons of tennis skill--but
that's a feature, not a bug.

I think it's great that there are some more achievable goals for people
to shoot for, but ultimately the tournament is the yearly chance for
the top players to get some recognition and showcase their skill, and
if there's going to be a lot of effort expended in an area I'd rather
see it put into highlighting Marvin, Rast, sawtooth, etc than
highlighting lesser players.



